# AI Readiness Guidelines

## Scope / Flexibility Notice
These guidelines establish patterns for implementing AI-ready architecture and integration points. While specific AI capabilities will evolve, these foundational principles should guide development.

## Best Practices
- Design pluggable AI service architecture
- Implement proper model versioning and updates
- Support both on-device and cloud AI processing
- Design fallbacks for when AI features are unavailable
- Implement proper user consent for AI features
- Design explainable AI interfaces for transparent user experience
- Support incremental AI feature adoption
- Implement proper telemetry for AI feature performance
- Design privacy-preserving AI features
- Implement energy-efficient AI processing strategies
- Support model personalization when appropriate

## File / Project Structure Guidelines
- Organize AI-related components:
  ```
  lib/
    core/
      ai/
        ai_service.dart
        ai_manager.dart
        model_loader.dart
        inference_engine.dart
        providers/
          on_device_provider.dart
          cloud_provider.dart
        models/
          model_metadata.dart
          model_version.dart
    data/
      repositories/
        ai_repository_impl.dart
      datasources/
        ai_local_datasource.dart
        ai_remote_datasource.dart
    domain/
      repositories/
        ai_repository.dart
      entities/
        inference_result.dart
        model_config.dart
      usecases/
        text_suggestion_usecase.dart
        smart_reply_usecase.dart
        content_moderation_usecase.dart
    presentation/
      widgets/
        smart_reply_suggestions.dart
        ai_powered_input.dart
  ```

## Coding & Styling Conventions
- Use descriptive naming for AI features: `SmartReplySuggestions`, `ContentDetection`
- Implement clear interfaces for AI services: `AIServiceProvider`
- Design feature flags for AI capabilities: `config.enableSmartReplies`
- Use consistent naming for AI operations: `generateSuggestions()`, `moderateContent()`
- Document model requirements and limitations
- Implement proper error states for AI feature failures
- Use analytics tagging for AI-powered features

## Performance & Optimization Tips
- Implement model quantization for on-device processing
- Use isolates for CPU-intensive inference
- Implement proper caching of inference results
- Support incremental model loading and unloading
- Design batch processing for related inferences
- Balance response time vs accuracy based on context
- Implement model warm-up for frequently used features
- Support model switching based on device capabilities
- Optimize tensor operations for specific hardware
- Implement proper memory management for large models

## Testing & Validation Guidelines
- Test AI features with diverse inputs
- Implement A/B testing for AI features
- Validate AI feature performance on low-end devices
- Test AI features with different model versions
- Verify graceful degradation when AI services unavailable
- Test privacy compliance for AI features
- Implement evaluation metrics for AI model quality
- Test battery impact of AI features
- Verify accuracy across different user scenarios
- Implement sandbox testing for new AI models
